What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_current1_sys_calibration
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		On PM8226, writing 1 calibrates the gain and zero-current
		references and programs the volatile external-sense offset trim.
		Writing 0 does nothing. Calibration and current conversions are
		serialized. The driver verifies protected trim writes before
		publishing the matching software calibration cache.

		On failure the previous trim/cache are retained where possible.
		If hardware restoration fails, current reads return an error
		until a successful calibration. Raw reference reads remain
		available for recovery. No coulomb counter is reset by this
		attribute. Kernel consumers must retain a managed dependency
		on the IADC provider while using its extended channel callbacks.
